ScreenGrabCraft is a clean-room screen capture and annotation suite. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by or derived from TechSmith Snagit or any other screen capture product. Product names
mentioned in the documentation (to say what a feature corresponds to) are trademarks of their
owners.

Portions adapted from MailCraft

ScreenGrabCraft follows the architecture and conventions of MailCraft
(https://github.com/billsecond/mailcraft), itself following WordCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft). These parts started from MailCraft's source, which is
Copyright (c) 2026 the MailCraft contributors and licensed under the MIT License or the Apache
License, Version 2.0:

- workspace tooling: xtask (layers, assets, wasm, ci, version, ico), rustfmt and clippy settings,
  the lint set;
- packaging scripts and metadata for macOS, Windows, Linux, FreeBSD and the web (packaging/), and
  the release workflows (.github/workflows/);
- desktop plumbing: the Windows graphics-backend choice (crates/desktop/src/graphics.rs) and the
  shape of the logger and the one-instance hand-over;
- the app icon pipeline's tile geometry (xtask/src/icon.rs).

Bundled fonts: PatroneOS Sans and PatroneOS Mono, Copyright 2026 William Daugherty
(https://patroneos.com/fonts), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/).
